<title>FRANCE: New York top Paris aircargo originator Jan-May - ADP.</title>
<headline>New York top Paris aircargo originator Jan-May - ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top airport gateway for imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in January-May 1997.</p>
<p>The top 10 orignating airport gateways for ADP imports in January-May 1997, with the percentage change on the same period in 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>   1.  New York	14,752 tonnes	 (-12.1 pct))</p>
<p>   2.  Chicago	 11,768 tonnes	  (-0.3)</p>
<p>   3.  Tokyo	    8,988 tonnes	 (+49.6))</p>
<p>   4.  Hong Kong	8,012 tonnes	 (+12.9)</p>
<p>   5.  Montreal	 6,550 tonnes	  (-7.2)</p>
<p>   6.  Los Angeles    5,904 tonnes	 (-17.2)</p>
<p>   7.  Singapore	3,925 tonnes	 (+89.6)</p>
<p>   8.  Miami	    2,997 tonnes	  (-5.0)</p>
<p>   9.  Seoul	    2,684 tonnes	 (+24.5)</p>
<p>  10.  Casablanca     2,671 tonnes	 (-22.9)</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax +5017</p>
